From 5fe782fdaa236950c3f6db4b2307637e381eaced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:35:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban-sync): account chat-link reconciliation substeps
 [daveey]

Why: the idle kanban-sync-links family used 3.121% of one core in the
original read-only Mac window, entirely outside named loop scopes.
The existing unchanged-board skip still evaluates shared sources first,
so source inspection alone cannot identify the dominant cost.

Add nested accounting for the complete pass, shared source inventory,
configuration signature, board/input gates, backfill, planning, local and
ledger links, owner releases, existing rows, machine releases, chat
classification, owner links, and writes. Record unchanged board skips.
No cache, freshness, scheduling, release or write policy changes.

Proof: accounting tests fail behaviorally without scopes; the initial
instrumentation and all 22 links files passed (246 tests). Expanded
local/ledger/classification test fails on the initial instrumentation
with AssertionError: sync.links.local. Expanded GREEN: all 22 files,
246 tests passed, 0 failed (accounting-expanded-green.log; exit 0).
Full scripts/check --base origin/main passes on the expanded change.

This is the measurement stage, not a CPU reduction claim. The owning
card retains structural skip/invalidation tests and a read-only idle
Mac family measurement below 0.5% after the optimization.
